🔹 Find (with Path Compression)
static int find(int x) {
    if (parent[x] != x)
        parent[x] = find(parent[x]);
    return parent[x];
}


Finds ultimate parent

Compresses path → faster future queries

🔹 Union (by Rank)
if (rank[rootX] < rank[rootY])
    parent[rootX] = rootY;


Attaches smaller tree under larger tree

Avoids deep trees

🔹 Sorting Edges
edges.sort(Comparator.comparingInt(e -> e.weight));


Kruskal always processes edges from minimum weight

🔹 Core MST Logic
if (find(e.src) != find(e.dest)) {
    union(e.src, e.dest);
    mstWeight += e.weight;
}


If nodes are in different sets → safe to add edge

Prevents cycles

